# GJS style

Follow `docs/coding-practices.md`. Shell-change patterns are in `docs/patterns.md`.

- ESM. `gi://` imports first, then `resource:///`, then local modules.
- `const` and `let`, 4-space indent, leading `_` for private methods and fields.
- Return early from guard clauses. Use a large `if` only when both branches are the work.
- SOLID, detailed in `docs/coding-practices.md`. One reason to change per class and per JS file.
- Actors use `GObject.registerClass` and `_init`. Feature controllers stay plain classes.
- Log with `extension.getLogger()`. Do not use global `log()` or `console.log`.
- Timeouts use `GLib.timeout_add` and are removed with `GLib.source_remove` in `disable()`.
- User-visible strings use `gettext as _` from `resource:///org/gnome/shell/extensions/extension.js`.
- Start the file with `// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later`.

```javascript
// Bad
this._panel.connect('scroll-event', this._onScroll);

// Good
this._signals.connect(this._panel, 'scroll-event', () => this._onScroll());
```
